  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity </title>
<para>A school is holding a carnival and hopes to raise $500. Child tickets cost $3, and adult tickets cost $5. If the school sells \( x \) child tickets and \( y \) adult tickets, then the equation \( 3x + 5y = 500 \) expresses the fact that the school raised exactly $500 from ticket sales.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Solve the equation for \( x \).

  </item>
</list>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </problem><solution>
    Enter your answer here:
  
    <para>Compare your answer:
       
      \( x= \frac{500-5y}{3} \)
    </para>
  </solution></exercise>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Explain when it might be helpful to rewrite the equation this way.</item>
</list>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </problem><solution>
    Enter your answer here:
  
    <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. Solving for \(x\) helps us find out the number of child tickets to sell if we know the number of adults attending the carnival and we want to make exactly $500 from ticket sales.
    </para>
  </solution></exercise></section>
</content>
